# Cloudflare Pages / Workers Assets redirect rules.
# Format: <from>  <to>  <status>

# Trailing-slash convention: the portal generates all internal links WITH a
# trailing slash (client.config.json pages[], nav.js topnav, index.html hrefs, and
# worker.js normUrl). Cloudflare Workers Assets html_handling (auto-trailing-slash)
# already serves '/roadmap/' -> '/roadmap/index.html' (200) and canonicalizes the
# slash-less '/roadmap' -> '/roadmap/' for free, matching that convention. So no
# trailing-slash rule is needed here — a strip-the-slash 308 would 308 AWAY from the
# exact URLs the app emits on every navigation, which is backwards.
